<h2 id="imperia-expanded">Imperia — Full Article Expansion</h2>
<div class="infobox">
<img src="images/imperia.png" alt="Imperia">
<b>Imperia</b><br>
Aliases: Imp, Old Man, Unc, Demon Guy<br>
Gender: Male<br>
Species: Reaper (Feline)<br>
Status: Alive (formerly deceased)<br>
Age: 35 (5 human years)<br>
Religion: Atheist (formerly Skankian)<br>
Ability: Metaphysical Foresight<br>
Cause of Mortal Death: Accidental drowning (sea storm)<br>
Residence: The Rift (current), The Void (former prisoner), Earth (former mortal)<br>
</div>
<p><b>Imperia</b>, most commonly referred to as <b>Imp</b>, is a central deuteragonist in <i>Twelve:AU</i> and <i>Rebirth?</i> Parts 1 and 2, and the anti-hero protagonist of <i>Rebirth?</i> Part 3. He is widely regarded as one of the most morally complex and narratively significant figures in the Twelve:AU universe.</p>

<h3>Overview</h3>
<p>Imp is neither a hero nor a villain. While he frequently commits ethically reprehensible acts—particularly manipulation, deception, and violations of the Reaper Code—he does so under the belief that his actions ultimately protect those he cares about. This belief, however, is consistently challenged by the harm his interference causes.</p>

<h3>Personality</h3>
<p>Imp is charismatic, witty, and outwardly laid-back, often presenting himself as a humorous and approachable figure. Beneath this exterior lies a deeply manipulative individual who rationalizes harmful behavior as necessary. He is self-aware of his moral failings but unwilling to meaningfully change, instead relying on charm to deflect accountability.</p>
<p>His relationship with May exemplifies this dynamic. Though platonic, it is widely considered predatory due to the significant age gap, power imbalance, and emotional manipulation involved. Both characters perceive the relationship as harmless, and the narrative intentionally reflects their perspectives, glossing over its troubling implications.</p>

<h3>Relationships</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>May</b> – Closest companion; emotionally dependent and frequently manipulated.</li>
<li><b>Ollie</b> – Second-closest friend prior to death.</li>
<li><b>Kate</b> – Considered a friend; treated with guarded respect.</li>
<li><b>Simon</b> – Complicated; tolerated more than trusted.</li>
<li><b>Devo</b> – Preferred over Simon due to optimism.</li>
<li><b>Princess</b> – Distant but acknowledged as part of his circle.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Religious Views</h3>
<p>Imp was raised Skankian but abandoned all religious belief after becoming a reaper, citing firsthand knowledge of the afterlife as incompatible with faith systems.</p>

